SECTION 1 (amending O.C.G.A. 16-11-127.1(b)(2)): "(2) Except as provided for in paragraph (20) of subsection (c) of this Code section, any Any license holder who violates this subsection shall be guilty of a misdemeanor.
SECTION 1 (amending O.C.G.A. 16-11-127.1(c)(20)): "(20)(A) Any weapons carry license holder when he or she is in any building or on real property owned by or leased to any public technical school, vocational school, college, or university, or other public institution of postsecondary education; provided, however, that such exception shall:
SECTION 1 (amending O.C.G.A. 16-11-127.1(c)(20)): (i) Not apply to buildings or property used for athletic sporting events or student housing, including, but not limited to, fraternity and sorority houses;
SECTION 1 (amending O.C.G.A. 16-11-127.1(c)(20)): (ii) Not apply to any preschool or childcare space located within such buildings or real property;
SECTION 1 (amending O.C.G.A. 16-11-127.1(c)(20)): (v) Not apply to faculty, staff, or administrative offices or rooms where disciplinary proceedings are conducted;
SECTION 1 (amending O.C.G.A. 16-11-127.1(c)(20)): (vii) Only apply to the carrying of handguns which are concealed.
SECTION 1 (amending O.C.G.A. 16-11-127.1(c)(20)): (B) Any weapons carry license holder who carries a handgun in a manner or in a building, property, room, or space in violation of this paragraph shall be guilty of a misdemeanor; provided, however, that for a conviction of a first offense, such weapons carry license holder shall be punished by a fine of $25.00 and not be sentenced to serve any term of confinement.
